# Business Idea — DonateNow

> Phase: 01 — Foundation
> Next: [PRD.mdc](./PRD.mdc)

---

## 1. Business Idea

**DonateNow** — A simple, transparent digital donation platform for local NGOs.

---

## 2. Problem Identified

A local NGO currently receives donations through **bank transfers** and struggles to:
- Track donor information (who donated, how much, when)
- Provide donors a seamless giving experience
- Generate reports for transparency and compliance
- Scale donation collection beyond manual processes

### Current Process (As-Is)
```
Donor contacts NGO
  → NGO shares bank account details manually
    → Donor makes bank transfer
      → NGO manually checks bank statement
        → NGO manually records donor info in spreadsheet
          → No thank-you or receipt sent automatically
```

### Pain Points
| # | Pain Point | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | No centralized donor tracking | Donor data lost, no follow-up possible |
| 2 | Manual bank statement reconciliation | Time-consuming, error-prone |
| 3 | No instant confirmation to donor | Poor donor experience, trust issues |
| 4 | No donation page | NGO cannot share a single link for donations |
| 5 | No reporting capability | Cannot show transparency to stakeholders |

---

## 3. Proposed Solution

Build a **simple donation platform** with:
1. A **public donation page** displaying the cause and predefined amounts
2. **Razorpay payment integration** for instant, secure payments
3. A **thank-you page** after successful donation
4. An **admin panel** for the NGO team to view donor details

### Future Process (To-Be)
```
NGO shares donation link
  → Donor visits donation page
    → Donor selects amount + fills info
      → Donor pays via Razorpay (card/UPI/netbanking)
        → Thank-you page displayed instantly
          → Donation auto-recorded in database
            → Admin views donor log anytime
```

---

## 4. Target Users

| User Type | Description | Actions |
|---|---|---|
| **Donor** | General public, supporters, well-wishers | View cause, donate, receive confirmation |
| **NGO Admin** | NGO team members managing donations | Login, view donor log, track totals |

---

## 5. Business Goals

| # | Goal | Metric |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Digitize donation collection | 100% donations via platform |
| 2 | Eliminate manual tracking | Zero spreadsheet dependency |
| 3 | Improve donor experience | Thank-you page within 3 seconds |
| 4 | Enable donor transparency | Admin dashboard with real-time data |
| 5 | Provide a shareable donation link | Single URL for all donation campaigns |

---

## 6. Core Features (High Level)

| # | Feature | User | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Public Donation Page | Donor | P0 — Must Have |
| 2 | Razorpay Payment Integration | Donor | P0 — Must Have |
| 3 | Thank-You Page | Donor | P0 — Must Have |
| 4 | Admin Login | Admin | P0 — Must Have |
| 5 | Admin Dashboard (Stats) | Admin | P1 — Important |
| 6 | Donor Log Table | Admin | P0 — Must Have |

---

## 7. Suggested Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Frontend + Backend | Next.js | Full-stack, SSR, API routes, fast |
| Database + Auth | Supabase | PostgreSQL, built-in auth, RLS, free tier |
| Payments | Razorpay (Test Mode) | India-focused, easy integration, test mode available |
| Hosting | Vercel | Free, seamless Next.js deployment |

---

## 8. Demo Scenario

```
1. A user visits the donation page
2. Selects ₹500 as donation amount
3. Fills in name and email
4. Clicks "Donate Now"
5. Completes payment via Razorpay Checkout
6. Thank-you page is displayed with donation details
7. Admin logs into admin panel
8. Admin sees the ₹500 donation in the donor log
```

---

## 9. Success Criteria

- [ ] Payment flow works successfully in test mode
- [ ] Thank-you page is displayed after donation
- [ ] Admin can view the donor log

---

## 10. Constraints

- MVP scope only — no recurring donations, no receipt generation, no multi-cause support
- Test mode only — no real money processed during development
- Single admin role — no role hierarchy
- No mobile app — web only

